### 5.1 Recording rule (to be finalised by A2/A3)
A row is an **x402 NEAR payment** only when all hold: transfer executed successfully and final; token contract == `NEAR_USDC_CONTRACT`; receiver == a watched `payto`; the receipt is a single `ft_transfer` with exactly one NEP-141 transfer event. **No memo is required or read**: the x402 NEAR exact scheme's transfer is `ft_transfer {receiver_id, amount}` inside a NEP-366 delegate and defines no memo (chainiam-private-ai `docs/NEAR-GATES.md` G3; the live payment `H3ZFsVY1zDSQKsL3dktYBcNHSLiE8GpR5JtytFLjnbqD` has none). A memo, when present, is kept as data only. Other transfers to the pay-to are listed as `unwatched` / `manual`, never counted — same policy as ledger-watch `seller.ts`.

### 5.2 Roads
| Road | Adapter | Kind |
|---|---|---|
| `neardata` | `feeds/neardata.ts` | long-poll by height (push-like) |
| `qn-rpc` | `feeds/quicknode-rpc.ts` | poll `block`/`chunk` every `--poll-sec` |
| `rpc` | `feeds/rpc-poll.ts` | public fallback |
| `backfill` | `backfill.ts` | from stored cursor after (re)start |
Road names are stored in SQLite and never renamed. A network reset (height far below stored cursor, `--reset-blocks`) stops the road with alert `network_reset`, as in ledger-watch.

### 5.3 Claims & reconcile
Same claim contract as ledger-watch (`payment_settled` line with `invoiceId`). Join claim ↔ chain transfer by **(network, tx hash) only** (base58, exact). The claim's `invoiceId` is shown when the claim has it and is never compared with a memo (an x402 NEAR transfer has none, chainiam-private-ai `docs/NEAR-GATES.md` G3). Amount (base units), payer and token are compared. States and alerts identical to ledger-watch; grace counted in final blocks (`--settle-grace-blocks`).

